Hmmm. On one hand, I understand the irritation about receiving weapons
when trying to go weaponless. On the other hand, having monks as a
class never get weapons semi-enforces the no-weapon conduct; it at
least makes it nearly impossible for a monk character to obtain a good
artifact weapon, should he wish to use one, unless he happens to see
it simply lying around somewhere. (I suppose he could still wish for
one.)

Maybe it would be more balanced to have the game check the flag for
"You have never hit with a wielded weapon" before granting an artifact
weapon (regardless of role). This goes against your appropriate
comment that conducts are completely voluntary and the game shouldn't
respond to them; however, it would have absolutely no effect on the
vast majority of games, and yet avoid handicapping characters trying
to go weaponless. (I say "handicapping" because when the player gets a
useless object from a sacrifice, the effect is a net loss, because he
suffers from a prayer timeout without gaining anything useful in
return.)
